				<div id="bodyContent" class="vector-body" aria-labelledby="firstHeading" data-mw-ve-target-container>
					<div class="vector-body-before-content">
							<div class="mw-indicators">
		</div>

						<div id="siteSub" class="noprint">From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</div>
						<div id="contentSub"><div id="mw-content-subtitle"></div></div>
						
					</div>
					
					<div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content"><div class="mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang="en" dir="ltr" data-mw-parsoid-version="0.24.0.0-alpha27" data-mw-html-version="2.8.0"><section data-mw-section-id="0" id="mwAQ"><div class="shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux" style="display:none" about="#mwt1" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Short description","href":"./Template:Short_description"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Social status concept"}},"i":0}}]}'>Social status concept</div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_short_description"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Short_description_matches_Wikidata"/></span>
<figure class="mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Frameless" id="mwAw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Horizontal_mobility_pyramid_II.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Horizontal_mobility_pyramid_II.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Horizontal_mobility_pyramid_II.svg/330px-Horizontal_mobility_pyramid_II.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Horizontal_mobility_pyramid_II.svg/960px-Horizontal_mobility_pyramid_II.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="512" data-file-height="512" data-file-type="drawing" height="300" width="300" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwBg"></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBw"><b id="mwCA">Horizontal mobility</b> is the mobility of the individual or group in the same <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_class" title="Social class" id="mwCQ">social class</a>, in the same situation category, without changing the level of power or status.<sup about="#mwt2" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchaefer201224_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESchaefer201224"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchaefer201224-1"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Schaefer"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"p":{"wt":"24"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchaefer201224-1" id="mwCg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Horizontal mobility, which is a type of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_mobility" title="Social mobility" id="mwDg">social mobility</a>, refers to the change of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Physical_space" title="Physical space" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDw">physical space</a> or profession without changes in the economic situation, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prestige_(sociolinguistics)" title="Prestige (sociolinguistics)" id="mwEA">prestige</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lifestyle_(sociology)" title="Lifestyle (sociology)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEQ">lifestyle</a> of the individual, or the forward or backward movement from one similar group or status to another.<sup about="#mwt5" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchaefer201224_1-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESchaefer201224"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchaefer201224-1"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Schaefer"},"2":{"wt":"2012"},"p":{"wt":"24"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchaefer201224-1" id="mwEg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwFg" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwFw" aria-labelledby="Definition"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Definition">Definition</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Horizontal_mobility&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Definition"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwGA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pitirim_Sorokin" title="Pitirim Sorokin" id="mwGQ">Pitirim Sorokin</a> defines horizontal mobility as a change in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Religion" title="Religion" id="mwGg">religious</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Region" title="Region" id="mwGw">regional</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Politics" title="Politics" id="mwHA">political</a>, or other horizontal shifts without any change in vertical position.<sup about="#mwt8" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTELind1928847_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTELind1928847"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELind1928847-2"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Lind"},"2":{"wt":"1928"},"p":{"wt":"847"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTELind1928847-2" id="mwHQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHw">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIA">]</span></span></a></sup>According to Andrew W. Lind, horizontal mobility occurs when a person changes their profession, but their <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_status" title="Social status" id="mwIQ">social status</a> remains unchanged. E.g. if a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_of_Medicine" title="Doctor of Medicine" id="mwIg">doctor</a> switches from a job in health care to teaching in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medical_school" title="Medical school" id="mwIw">medical school</a>, the profession changes, but dignity and social status remain the same.<sup about="#mwt11" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTELind1928412_3-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTELind1928412"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELind1928412-3"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Lind"},"2":{"wt":"1928"},"p":{"wt":"412"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTELind1928412-3" id="mwJA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJg">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJw">]</span></span></a></sup> According to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cameron_Anderson_(psychologist)?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Cameron Anderson (psychologist) (page does not exist)" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" id="mwKA" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Cameron Anderson (psychologist)"]}}'>Cameron Anderson</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_status" title="Social status" id="mwKQ">social status</a> is the level of social value that a person is considered to have.<sup about="#mwt14" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAndersonHildrethHowland2015574–601_4-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEAndersonHildrethHowland2015574–601"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAndersonHildrethHowland2015574–601-4"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Anderson"},"2":{"wt":"Hildreth"},"3":{"wt":"Howland"},"4":{"wt":"2015"},"pp":{"wt":"574–601"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAndersonHildrethHowland2015574–601-4" id="mwKg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLA">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The American sociologist <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linda_K._George" title="Linda K. George" id="mwLg">Linda K. George</a> listed the social status factors in horizontal mobility as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Work_(human_activity)" title="Work (human activity)" id="mwLw">work</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wealth" title="Wealth" id="mwMA">wealth</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Success_(concept)" title="Success (concept)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwMQ">success</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Education" title="Education" id="mwMg">education</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethnicity" title="Ethnicity" id="mwMw">ethnicity</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marital_status" title="Marital status" id="mwNA">marital status</a>.<sup about="#mwt17" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGeorge1978840–847_5-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEGeorge1978840–847"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGeorge1978840–847-5"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"George"},"2":{"wt":"1978"},"pp":{"wt":"840–847"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGeorge1978840–847-5" id="mwNQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNw">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwOQ" aria-labelledby="Timeline"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Timeline">Timeline</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Horizontal_mobility&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Timeline"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwOg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pitirim_Sorokin" title="Pitirim Sorokin" id="mwOw">Pitirim Sorokin</a> defined <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_mobility" title="Social mobility" id="mwPA">social mobility</a> between positions as two types: vertical and horizontal. According to Sorokin, the first period in which horizontal mobility tended to increase was the second half of the nineteenth century.<sup about="#mwt20" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTESorokin1959381_6-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTESorokin1959381"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESorokin1959381-6"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Sorokin"},"2":{"wt":"1959"},"p":{"wt":"381"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTESorokin1959381-6" id="mwPQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPw">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQA">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academic_studies" title="Academic studies" class="mw-redirect" id="mwQQ">Academic studies</a> have been carried out on the direction of the movement that will maintain and improve this distinction made by Sorokin. The vertical or horizontal <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_mobility" title="Social mobility" id="mwQg">social mobility</a> that a person shows in his own life is called intragenerational mobility.<sup about="#mwt23" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKemerlioglu1996148_7-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEKemerlioglu1996148"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKemerlioglu1996148-7"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Kemerlioglu"},"2":{"wt":"1996"},"p":{"wt":"148"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKemerlioglu1996148-7" id="mwQw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwRA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRQ">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRg">]</span></span></a></sup> According to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Max_Weber" title="Max Weber" id="mwRw">Weber</a>, when mobility changes, up or down, class conflicts lose their central importance and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Group_solidarity" title="Group solidarity" class="mw-redirect" id="mwSA">group solidarity</a> gives way to competition.<sup about="#mwt26" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAberg1979249_8-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEAberg1979249"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAberg1979249-8"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Aberg"},"2":{"wt":"1979"},"p":{"wt":"249"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAberg1979249-8" id="mwSQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwSg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSw">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTA">]</span></span></a></sup> According to the conflict theorists, the diversification of social roles due to competition and industrialization led to the emergence of horizontal mobility.<sup about="#mwt29" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAberg1979249_8-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEAberg1979249"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAberg1979249-8"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Aberg"},"2":{"wt":"1979"},"p":{"wt":"249"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAberg1979249-8" id="mwTQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTw">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwUQ" aria-labelledby="Metrology"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Metrology">Metrology</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Horizontal_mobility&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Metrology"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwUg">Horizontal mobility is one of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantitative_research" title="Quantitative research" id="mwUw">quantitative research</a> methods. Werrett Wallace Charters conducted a horizontal mobility study on American teachers called "The Social Background of Teaching".<sup about="#mwt32" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTECharters1963753_9-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTECharters1963753"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECharters1963753-9"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Charters"},"2":{"wt":"1963"},"p":{"wt":"753"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTECharters1963753-9" id="mwVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwVQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVg">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVw">]</span></span></a></sup> John W. Alspaugh from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Missouri" title="University of Missouri" id="mwWA">University of Missouri</a> referred to the Charters, in his research called  <i id="mwWQ">An Index of Teacher Horizontal Mobility,</i>  "The properties of horizontal mobility and attempting to measure it arose from an interest in testing research hypotheses regarding the mobility of various types of educators."<sup about="#mwt35" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19695–8_10-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19695–8"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19695–8-10"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Alspaugh"},"2":{"wt":"1969"},"pp":{"wt":"5-8"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19695–8-10" id="mwWg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwWw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXA">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Alspaugh, developed formulas for measuring the horizontal mobility of teachers.<sup about="#mwt38" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19697_11-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19697"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19697-11"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Alspaugh"},"2":{"wt":"1969"},"p":{"wt":"7"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19697-11" id="mwXg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwXw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYA">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwYg" aria-labelledby="Works"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Works">Works</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Horizontal_mobility&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Works"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwYw" aria-labelledby="Teacher_mobility_study"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Teacher_mobility_study">Teacher mobility study</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Horizontal_mobility&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Teacher mobility study"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwZA">The goal of Alspaugh's study was to develop an index of teacher mobility that would be used as research.<sup about="#mwt41" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19696_12-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19696"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19696-12"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Alspaugh"},"2":{"wt":"1969"},"p":{"wt":"6"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19696-12" id="mwZQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwZg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZw">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
