<blockquote id="mwug"><p id="mwuw">For the mobility index to be valid, the trainer must have accepted the general mobility concept. The table above is a ranking of the 3 career orders from least to most.<sup about="#mwt44" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19697_11-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19697"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19697-11"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Alspaugh"},"2":{"wt":"1969"},"p":{"wt":"7"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAlspaugh19697-11" id="mwvA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwvQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvg">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvw">]</span></span></a></sup></p></blockquote>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwwA" aria-labelledby="The_Power_Elite"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="The_Power_Elite">The Power Elite</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Horizontal_mobility&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: The Power Elite"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwwQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Power_Elite" title="The Power Elite" id="mwwg">The Power Elite</a> is a book published in 1956 by the American sociologist <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C._Wright_Mills" title="C. Wright Mills" id="mwww">C. Wright Mills</a>.<sup about="#mwt47" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMills19991_13-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEMills19991"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMills19991-13"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Mills"},"2":{"wt":"1999"},"p":{"wt":"1"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMills19991-13" id="mwxA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwxQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxg">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxw">]</span></span></a></sup> In this book, Mills dealt with the horizontal mobility of the relationship between the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Political" title="Political" class="mw-redirect" id="mwyA">political</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military" title="Military" id="mwyQ">military</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economy" title="Economy" id="mwyg">economic</a> elites. Mills has written that horizontal mobility moves within and between three institutional structures.<sup about="#mwt50" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEJohnson1997785–786_14-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEJohnson1997785–786"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEJohnson1997785–786-14"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Johnson"},"2":{"wt":"1997"},"pp":{"wt":"785–786"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEJohnson1997785–786-14" id="mwyw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwzA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzQ">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section></section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwzw" aria-labelledby="References"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="References">References</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Horizontal_mobility&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: References"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

